# Attendance + Desktop CRM (agent constraints)

## Policies (source of truth in code)

- `apps/web/src/lib/attendance-policy.ts`
  - `ATTENDANCE_TAB_CLOSE_ENABLED = false` (browser tab-close compliance off)
  - Laptop sleep detect (web note threshold): 6 minutes
  - Cursor idle: disabled
- `apps/desktop/src/shared/config.ts`
  - Laptop sleep/lock **detect delay**: 2 minutes (requires new desktop installer for employees)

## Product behavior

- Sleep and Lock are the same unscheduled cause: `sleep`.
- Official/manual Break open → do not open Sleep/Lock away on top.
- Desktop window close while shift open hides to tray; monitoring continues (not tab-close).

## Delivery

- Web-only changes: push `main` → Vercel.
- Electron shell / desktop monitor thresholds: rebuild via **Desktop Release** workflow; do not claim auto-update is complete unless `DESKTOP_UPDATE_URL` / GitHub provider is fully wired and verified.
- Employee install page must keep a working CTA (middleware HTML fallback + GitHub Releases asset name with **dots**: `AsbaTechs.CRM.Setup.0.1.0.exe`).
- When production “looks old”, compare the host under test (`*.vercel.app` vs custom domain) — stale custom DNS is a common cause.

## Desktop installer CRM URL (mandatory)

- Secret `CRM_APP_URL` for Desktop Release: **`https://asbatechs-crm-web.vercel.app`** (no trailing slash).
- Wrong secret → employees see **old UI** even when `/download/desktop` on Vercel looks new.
- After every Desktop Release: scan latest Setup `.exe` for that Vercel host before telling the user employees are fixed.
- Local `AppData/.../crm-app.url` overrides only **this PC**; it does not fix employee installers.
- Old PowerShell agent (`ASBA Attendance Agent`): **disable / comment**, do not delete files, when Desktop monitoring is primary.
